# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — NovaFabric
# Universal build/junk/secret rules honoured by EVERY git operating in this tree
# (the public .git and the private .git-private share this one working tree).
#
# NOTE: private material (design/, monetize/, bench/, site-config/, .claude/,
# CLAUDE.md, THREAT_MODEL.md, …) is NOT listed here on purpose — it is versioned
# in the private git and kept out of the public remote by the repo-local
# allowlist in .git/info/exclude.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.local
*.pem
*.key
.envrc
credentials.json
# Dashboard showcase fixture that embeds an Ed25519 private half. It is denied
# in .dualgit/private.deny, but the `web/src/data` carve-out is emitted AFTER
# the denies in .git/info/exclude and git's last-matching rule wins, so the deny
# was silently overridden and `git add -A` staged the key into a public commit
# (caught by `dualgit doctor`, never pushed). This rule sits in .gitignore
# because .gitignore outranks .git/info/exclude, so no carve-out can re-expose
# it. The private git already tracks the file, and an ignore rule never untracks.
web/src/data/fixtures/evidence-bundle/demo-key.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.pypirc

